---
import SpikeTable from './SpikeTable.astro';
import { csvUrl, type EditionRow } from '../lib/spike-edition';
interface Props { rows: EditionRow[] }
const { rows } = Astro.props;
const concentrated = rows.filter(r => r.total >= 100).sort((a,b) => b.share-a.share || a.slug.localeCompare(b.slug));
const examples = ['hermes','nullclaw'].map(slug => rows.find(row => row.slug === slug)!);
---
<section id="after-the-spike" aria-labelledby="edition-title" class="mb-12">
  <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ledger-red">OpenClaw ecosystem analysis · October 8 – November 6, 2026</p>
  <h1 id="edition-title" class="mt-3 mb-4">After the spike</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-ledger-muted max-w-2xl">Of the stars {examples[0].name} added in the study period, {examples[0].share.toFixed(1)}% came on its three busiest days. For {examples[1].name} the same three-day measure was {examples[1].share.toFixed(1)}%. Looking at the rest of the month shows how long that attention lasted.</p>
  <div class="examples">{examples.map(row => <div>
    <span>{row.name}</span><b>{row.share.toFixed(1)}%</b>
    <div class="track"><i style={`width:${row.share}%`}></i></div>
    <small>{row.top.toLocaleString('en-US')} of {row.total.toLocaleString('en-US')} additions on its three busiest days</small>
  </div>)}</div>
  <div class="ranking">
    <h2>Where did the attention go?</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ledger-muted mt-1"><span class="daily-note">Each square is one day, shaded relative to this agent’s busiest day.</span><span class="weekly-note">Each block shows the average stars per day for one week, shaded relative to this agent’s busiest week. The last block covers two days.</span> Compare totals to see the difference in audience size.</p>
    <div class="scale" aria-hidden="true">Zero <i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i> Busiest period for that row</div>
    <fieldset><legend class="sr-only">Rank projects by</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="spike-ranking" value="volume" checked /> Most stars added</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="spike-ranking" value="share" /> Highest three-day share</label>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="volume"><SpikeTable rows={rows.slice(0,8)} caption="Top eight by stars added during the month." /></div>
    <div class="share"><SpikeTable rows={concentrated.slice(0,8)} caption={`Top eight by concentration among the ${concentrated.length} projects with at least 100 additions.`} /></div>
    <details><summary>Explore all {rows.length} repositories with history</summary><SpikeTable rows={rows} caption="All repositories with daily history, ordered by stars added." /></details>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-ledger-muted">Atomic Agent attracted stars on every day of the study. Of its 537 additions, 206 came on its three busiest days. Use the daily pattern to decide which projects deserve a closer look. Stars alone can’t tell you what caused a spike or how many people kept using an agent.</p>
  <details class="method"><summary>Method and downloads</summary>
    <p>For each project, divide the stars added on its three busiest days by all additions over the 30-day window. Those days can be nonconsecutive. GitHub reports when people who still star a repository clicked the star button. Someone who starred and later unstarred before November 7 disappears from this history. Six projects had 30 measured days with zero additions. We kept all six. ApexClaw had no history available and was excluded from this edition.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2"><a href={csvUrl} download>Daily data (CSV)</a><a href="/analysis/data/three-day-share.svg" download>Comparison figure (SVG)</a><a href="/methodology/#star-history">How we measure stars</a></div>
  </details>
</section>
<style>
  p{max-width:74ch}
  .examples{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1px;border-radius:1rem;overflow:hidden;background:#557166;color:#fffaf0;margin:1.4rem 0}
  .examples>div{background:var(--field-ink,#124e43);padding:clamp(.9rem,2.3vw,1.6rem)}.examples span{font-weight:600}
  .examples b{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4.8vw,3.25rem);line-height:1.15;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .examples small{display:block;margin-top:.6rem;color:#e0e9df;line-height:1.4}
  .track{height:.4rem;background:#416755;border-radius:1rem;margin-top:.65rem}.track i{display:block;background:#f6c587;height:100%;border-radius:inherit}
  .ranking{background:#fffdf8;border:1px solid #ded8ca;padding:clamp(.85rem,2vw,1.6rem);border-radius:1rem}
  fieldset{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.75rem;margin:.95rem 0 .25rem}label{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem;font-size:.85rem;cursor:pointer}input{accent-color:#50483e}label{min-height:44px}
  .scale{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.23rem;margin-top:.7rem;font-size:.78rem;color:#565951}.scale i{width:.7rem;height:.7rem;background:#e8e6d9}.scale i:nth-of-type(2){background:#c8ddc6}.scale i:nth-of-type(3){background:#93baa1}.scale i:nth-of-type(4){background:#4b917b}.scale i:nth-of-type(5){background:#216351}
  .weekly-note{display:none}@media(max-width:480px){.weekly-note{display:inline}.daily-note{display:none}}
  .share{display:none}.ranking:has(input[value=share]:checked) .share{display:block}.ranking:has(input[value=share]:checked) .volume{display:none}
  details{margin-top:1rem}summary,.method a{font-weight:600;color:var(--field-ink,#124e43);cursor:pointer}.method{font-size:.9rem}.method p{margin:.6rem 0}.method a{text-decoration:underline}
</style>
